<% content_for :title, "Your Library" %>

<div class="px-4 pb-10 sm:px-8">
  <%# Records on their way to the disk.
      They are drawn here, above everything, because in the only sense that matters
      they are already yours: somebody went and got them, and they are coming. Grey,
      with a clock and a number that climbs — they cannot be played, and they do not
      pretend they can.

      It is the loop the rest of this app opened, closing. The gap in the shelf was
      named; now it is being filled, and you can stand here and watch it. %>
  <%# The disk is full, so the chase has stopped. A library that fills its own disk
      stops being one — and an app that quietly stopped fetching, and let somebody
      wonder why, would be worse than one that never fetched at all. %>
  <% if @no_room && WantedRecord.still_missing.any? %>
    <p class="mb-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.03] px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-500 ring-1 ring-inset ring-white/10">
      <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-300"><%= @no_room %></span>
      There are <%= number_with_delimiter(WantedRecord.still_missing.count) %> records you play and don't own,
      and they're still on the list — <%= link_to "the report", report_path, class: "text-neutral-300 underline hover:text-white" %>
      names them. Make room and they'll start arriving.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <% if @coming.any? %>
    <div class="mb-10 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.03] p-5 ring-1 ring-inset ring-white/10">
      <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-neutral-300">
        <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-4 animate-pulse text-neutral-500" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor">
          <path d="M8 1.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Z"/>
          <path d="M8 3.75a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v3.06l2 1.16a.75.75 0 1 1-.75 1.3L7.62 8.9A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 8.25V4.5A.75.75 0 0 1 8 3.75Z"/>
        </svg>
        On the way
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-neutral-600">
        You play these and don't have them. They're being fetched — the scan will make them real.
      </p>

      <ul class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 xl:grid-cols-5">
        <% @coming.each do |record| %>
          <li>
            <div class="relative aspect-square overflow-hidden rounded bg-white/[0.03] ring-1 ring-inset ring-white/5">
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-full items-center justify-center">
                <svg class="size-8 text-neutral-800" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor">
                  <path d="M8 1.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Z"/>
                  <path d="M8 3.75a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v3.06l2 1.16a.75.75 0 1 1-.75 1.3L7.62 8.9A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 8.25V4.5A.75.75 0 0 1 8 3.75Z"/>
                </svg>
              </span>

              <%# The number that climbs. Without the client to ask, there is no
                  number — and the record is still coming, so it still shows. %>
              <% if record.progress %>
                <span class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-1 bg-black/40">
                  <span class="block h-full bg-neutral-500" style="width: <%= record.progress %>%"></span>
                </span>
              <% end %>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-3 truncate text-sm font-semibold text-neutral-500"><%= record.title %></p>
            <p class="truncate text-xs text-neutral-700"><%= record.artist %></p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs tabular-nums text-neutral-700">
              <%= record.progress ? "#{record.progress}%" : "Queued" %>
              · <%= number_with_delimiter(record.plays) %> plays
            </p>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <% if @recently_played.any? %>
    <h1 class="mb-4 mt-4 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl">Recently played</h1>

    <div class="mb-10 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 xl:grid-cols-5">
      <% @recently_played.each do |album| %>
        <%= link_to album_path(album), class: "group rounded-lg p-4 transition hover:bg-white/5" do %>
          <div class="aspect-square overflow-hidden rounded bg-neutral-800 shadow-lg">
            <%= render "shared/sleeve", album: album, size: 320,
                       class: "size-full object-cover transition duration-300 group-hover:scale-105" %>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 truncate text-base font-bold text-white"><%= album.title %></p>
          <p class="mt-1 truncate text-sm text-neutral-400"><%= album.artist.name %></p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# The same three turns as the rail, and the same control — one library, and
      you say which way you want to be shown it. %>
  <div data-controller="tabs" data-tabs-showing-value="artists" data-tabs-remember-value="mediateca:library-page">
    <div class="mb-6 mt-4 flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl">Your Library</h1>

      <div role="tablist" aria-label="Your Library" data-action="keydown->tabs#step"
           class="segmented flex w-40 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-black/30 p-1 ring-1 ring-inset ring-white/10">
        <%= render "shared/library_tabs", size: "size-5", pad: "py-2" %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Artists are round, records are square. You can tell a person from a sleeve
        without reading either. %>
    <div role="tabpanel" aria-label="Artists" data-tabs-target="panel" data-tabs-name="artists"
         class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 xl:grid-cols-5">
      <%# The menu sits *beside* the link, not inside it: a card is one big link to
          the artist, and a button inside a link is not a button.

          It is always there, and not revealed on hover: a phone has no hover, and
          a menu that only a pointer can summon is a menu half this app's screens
          cannot open at all. %>
      <% library_artists.each do |artist| %>
        <div class="group relative">
          <%= link_to artist_path(artist), class: "block rounded-lg p-4 transition hover:bg-white/5" do %>
            <div class="aspect-square overflow-hidden rounded-full bg-neutral-800 shadow-lg">
              <%= render "shared/artist_face", artist: artist, text: "text-5xl", size: 320 %>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-4 truncate text-center text-base font-bold text-white"><%= artist.name %></p>
            <p class="mt-1 truncate text-center text-sm text-neutral-400">
              <%= pluralize(artist.albums.size, "album") %>
            </p>
          <% end %>

          <div class="absolute right-2 top-2">
            <%= render "shared/standing", artist: artist %>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div role="tabpanel" aria-label="Albums" data-tabs-target="panel" data-tabs-name="albums" hidden
         class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 xl:grid-cols-5">
      <% library_albums.each do |album| %>
        <%= link_to album_path(album), class: "group rounded-lg p-4 transition hover:bg-white/5" do %>
          <div class="aspect-square overflow-hidden rounded bg-neutral-800 shadow-lg">
            <%= render "shared/sleeve", album: album, size: 320,
                       class: "size-full object-cover transition duration-300 group-hover:scale-105" %>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 truncate text-base font-bold text-white"><%= album.title %></p>
          <p class="mt-1 truncate text-sm text-neutral-400">
            <%= album.artist.name %><%= " · #{album.year}" if album.year %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div role="tabpanel" aria-label="Playlists" data-tabs-target="panel" data-tabs-name="playlists" hidden
         class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 xl:grid-cols-5">
      <%= link_to likes_path, class: "group rounded-lg p-4 transition hover:bg-white/5" do %>
        <div aria-hidden="true" class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded bg-gradient-to-br from-indigo-500 to-violet-700 shadow-lg">
          <svg class="size-12 text-white transition duration-300 group-hover:scale-110" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor">
            <path d="M8 14S1.5 9.7 1.5 5.6A3.6 3.6 0 0 1 8 3.5a3.6 3.6 0 0 1 6.5 2.1C14.5 9.7 8 14 8 14Z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 truncate text-base font-bold text-white">Liked Songs</p>
        <p class="mt-1 truncate text-sm text-neutral-400">
          <%= pluralize(Current.profile.liked_songs_count, "song") %>
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <% playlists.each do |playlist| %>
        <%= link_to playlist, class: "group rounded-lg p-4 transition hover:bg-white/5" do %>
          <div aria-hidden="true" class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded bg-neutral-800 text-neutral-300 shadow-lg ring-1 ring-inset ring-white/10">
            <svg class="size-12 transition duration-300 group-hover:scale-110" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor">
              <path d="M6 3h9v1.5H6V3ZM6 7h9v1.5H6V7ZM1 11h14v1.5H1V11ZM1 3h3v1.5H1V3ZM1 7h3v1.5H1V7Z"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 truncate text-base font-bold text-white"><%= playlist.name %></p>
          <p class="mt-1 truncate text-sm text-neutral-400"><%= pluralize(playlist_song_counts.fetch(playlist.id, 0), "song") %></p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%# A fresh install used to show that heading over nothing at all, which reads
        like a bug rather than an empty shelf. The music is on the disk; nothing
        has looked at it yet, and that is a sentence somebody can act on. %>
    <% if library_artists.empty? %>
      <div class="py-16 text-center">
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400">Nothing here yet.</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
          The catalog is filled by scanning the disk — <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-neutral-300">bin/kamal import</code>,
          or every night at four.
        </p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# Everybody this library does *not* have.
      Mediateca is a shelf of the records you own, and until now it could say
      nothing at all about the ones you do not: an import counted them, reported a
      number, and threw the names away. So it knew about a thousand songs somebody
      loves and could not name one of them.

      They are drawn the way they are because of what they are: no photograph,
      because nobody here has a record with their face on it; grey, because there
      is nothing to play; not clickable, because there is nowhere to go. This is a
      shopping list, and the only honest thing it can do is be legible. %>
  <% missing = Current.profile.absent_artists %>
  <% if missing.any? %>
    <div class="mt-14 border-t border-white/5 pt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-400 sm:text-2xl">Not here yet</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-neutral-600">
        You listen to these on Spotify. There isn't a record by them on the disk.
      </p>

      <ul class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 xl:grid-cols-5">
        <% missing.each do |stranger| %>
          <li class="rounded-lg p-4">
            <div aria-hidden="true"
                 class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white/[0.03] text-5xl font-bold text-neutral-800 ring-1 ring-inset ring-white/5">
              <%= stranger.name.first&.upcase %>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-4 truncate text-center text-base font-semibold text-neutral-500"><%= stranger.name %></p>
            <p class="mt-1 truncate text-center text-sm text-neutral-700">
              <%= pluralize(stranger.songs, "song") %> you don't have
            </p>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
